* Behavioral regulator macromodel for CI verification.
* This is NOT a vendor part model — it's an ideal voltage source (VSET) in
* series with an output resistance (RS) that stands in for load regulation,
* so we can assert "does this rail land in spec under load" in CI before a
* real IC is chosen. Swap for a real vendor SPICE model once U1/U2 are
* selected, and update io_specs/power.yaml accordingly.
.subckt REG VIN GND VOUT PARAMS: VSET=5.0 RS=0.01
Eout VOUT_IDEAL GND VALUE = {VSET}
Rout VOUT_IDEAL VOUT {RS}
.ends REG
